  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 39,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/9997910480b256f833b9d43b60e8ad1d3354803b/docs%2Fdocs%2Freferences%2Fproduction_metrics.mdx",
      "changes": 39,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fdocs%2Freferences%2Fproduction_metrics.mdx?ref=9997910480b256f833b9d43b60e8ad1d3354803b",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/docs/references/production_metrics.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -115,6 +115,45 @@ sglang:spec_num_steps{model_name=\"meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct\"} 3.0\n sglang:spec_num_draft_tokens{model_name=\"meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct\"} 4.0\n ```\n \n+## Scheduler load and queueing\n+\n+Use these metrics alongside request latency to distinguish waiting requests from\n+active work. This is a focused operational reference, not an exhaustive list.\n+Availability depends on the enabled server features and workload.\n+\n+| Metric | Type | Meaning |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `sglang:num_running_reqs` | Gauge | Requests currently running in the scheduler. |\n+| `sglang:num_queue_reqs` | Gauge | Requests waiting for scheduling. |\n+| `sglang:gen_throughput` | Gauge | Reported generation rate in tokens per second. |\n+| `sglang:cache_hit_rate` | Gauge | Reported prefix-cache hit rate. |\n+| `sglang:num_used_tokens` | Gauge | Tokens currently using the KV pool. |\n+| `sglang:token_usage` | Gauge | Reported KV token capacity usage. |\n+| `sglang:queue_time_seconds` | Histogram | Time requests spend queued, in seconds. |\n+| `sglang:num_retracted_reqs` | Gauge | Reported retracted-request count. |\n+| `sglang:num_retracted_requests_total` | Counter | Cumulative request retractions. |\n+| `sglang:num_grammar_cache_hit_total` | Counter | Grammar-cache hits. |\n+\n+Use `rate()` with counters to measure changes over time. Gauges describe reported\n+state and must not be treated as cumulative counters. For example:\n+\n+```promql\n+sum(rate(sglang:num_retracted_requests_total[5m]))\n+```\n+\n+To inspect queueing latency, aggregate histogram buckets while retaining `le`:\n+\n+```promql\n+histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(sglang:queue_time_seconds_bucket[5m])))\n+```\n+\n+These queries combine all selected series. Add label filters or grouping for the\n+model and scheduler replicas you want to compare. Inspect your `/metrics` output\n+for the labels your deployment exports before copying a dashboard query.\n+\n+The names and types are defined in\n+[`metrics_collector.py`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/python/sglang/srt/observability/metrics_collector.py).\n+\n ## Request-level time per output token (TPOT)\n \n `sglang:request_time_per_output_token_seconds` records TPOT once per successfully finished request:",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/9997910480b256f833b9d43b60e8ad1d3354803b/docs%2Fdocs%2Freferences%2Fproduction_metrics.mdx",
      "sha": "314e15c7d4aa3de279b0dbd8780d35fc45bb4242",
      "status": "modified"
